{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head eae8a7019474406f4a7cd8c85bfaa04913b64318, on planner/subject-admission-20261114, its one artifact ad32737e (`notes/2026-11-14-subject-admission.md`), for request 1defd15d under my promise 8863ea2d. I approved the parent 7fdb7511 in 988f1055. This verdict covers the one commit that follows it.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- The diff from 7fdb7511. The status line and section 10 record the owner's decisions of 15 November. Section 7 drops the install gate. It states that a room at any Rules pin installs a definition with the part when its Worker's validator admits it. Two rules of operation replace the gate: every room Worker and verifier takes the step A2 head before an author publishes such a definition, and a Worker does not return to a head before step A2 after one of its rooms installs one. Section 9 removes the gate from step A2, rewrites case 9 as an install at an earlier Rules pin, and drops the gate control.\n- Kernel ruling 451d3c8e. It permits step A under sections 7 and 7.1 of `docs/kernel.md`, with no install gate, and it matches section 10 of the note.\n\nWhat I checked against the code:\n\n- No Rules version reads the admission. The install gate for reference fields lives in `packages/platform/src/application-install-reference.ts` and its three callers. The judge and the validator live in `packages/derive`, and the note puts the admission there.\n- A validator before step A2 refuses the part with `shape`. The top-level `rec` in `packages/derive/src/validate/index.ts:147` names `level` and `capacity` as the only optional parts. `rec` in `packages/derive/src/validate/shape.ts:61-66` refuses any other member with `shape` and \"is not a field or form the contract defines\". The act form at `packages/derive/src/validate/handlers.ts:231` refuses an unknown member such as `current` the same way.\n- The branch's merge base with main 9e42735a is 26d1e65c, and from there only this note changes. It merges into main with no conflict. The commit-message check passes: 5 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean. This is a notes-only head, so I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The admission is a property of the pinned definition, which the judge reads. A Rules pin governs install policy and has no part in it, so a gate tied to a pin would be an unrelated control.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding. Without the gate, a Worker or verifier that lacks the step A2 code refuses the definition with `shape`. It does not admit the definition and judge it wrong. The failure is a refusal, not a wrong answer. One fact for the record: the second rule of operation is a rollback limit. After a room installs a definition with the part, a Worker rolled back before step A2 refuses that room's pinned definition, and the room records nothing until the Worker moves forward again. No code enforces either rule. The step A2 deployment record must state the limit, as the note requires, and the deploy owner must check it before any rollback.\n\nSimplification: the head removes the gate, its reason name, its pin table and its control. One sentence explains why case 9 has no control.\n\nKernel: consistent with ruling 451d3c8e. Step A2 still has to write the ruling into sections 7 and 7.1 of the kernel page and add the part to promise 3.\n\nThis approval authorizes no build, landing or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ad32737e809ed95654cf6ee23a5f6dd288d0d53d","binding":"assigned","head":"eae8a7019474406f4a7cd8c85bfaa04913b64318","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8863ea2d006050306a864c29053fff42ea3a2be8\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:79b023ca9de287796ec5c23e6703be64f844cc37\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:790afe00333dd0cd581b78a61ce37e434074628c","review_path":"reviewg